WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.942
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:09.896
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:16.958
Unit thirteen: Phrasal Verbs and Idioms. Today you will understand common phrasal verbs and idioms in context.

4
00:00:17.258 --> 00:00:19.992
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.236
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:26.108
Phrasal verb.

7
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:29.673
Phrasal verb means a verb plus a particle.

8
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.039
Give up is a phrasal verb.

9
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.360
Your turn. Say: Phrasal verb.

10
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.387
Phrasal verb.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:40.954
Idiom.

12
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.926
Idiom means a fixed expression.

13
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:45.773
It is an idiom.

14
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:49.105
Your turn. Say: Idiom.

15
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:52.921
Idiom.

16
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:54.452
Give up.

17
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.194
Give up means to stop trying.

18
00:00:57.783 --> 00:00:58.877
Never give up.

19
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:02.170
Your turn. Say: Give up.

20
00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:05.860
Give up.

21
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:07.618
Look after.

22
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:10.709
Look after means to take care of.

23
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:12.817
She looks after her brother.

24
00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:16.220
Your turn. Say: Look after.

25
00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.184
Look after.

26
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:21.765
Carry on.

27
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.448
Carry on means to continue.

28
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.423
Carry on working.

29
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.414
Your turn. Say: Carry on.

30
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.372
Carry on.

31
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:35.002
Turn down.

32
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:37.703
Turn down means to refuse.

33
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:39.771
He turned down the offer.

34
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:42.653
Your turn. Say: Turn down.

35
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.594
Turn down.

36
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.607
Break the ice.

37
00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:52.092
Break the ice means to start a conversation.

38
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:54.416
A joke broke the ice.

39
00:01:55.017 --> 00:01:58.029
Your turn. Say: Break the ice.

40
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:02.112
Break the ice.

41
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.165
A piece of cake.

42
00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.370
A piece of cake means very easy.

43
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:09.693
The test was a piece of cake.

44
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:13.168
Your turn. Say: A piece of cake.

45
00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.441
A piece of cake.

46
00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:21.965
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:24.967
Visal, what is a phrasal verb?

48
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:34.959
It is a verb with a particle such as up, off or after, and the meaning is often different from the verb alone. Give up means stop trying.

49
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.295
Can I separate them?

50
00:02:38.383 --> 00:02:53.043
Some can be separated: turn the offer down. When the object is a pronoun, it must go in the middle: turn it down, not turn down it. Others, like look after, cannot be separated.

51
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.546
What about idioms?

52
00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:07.711
An idiom has a fixed meaning that is not literal. Break the ice means start a friendly conversation. Use idioms carefully and learn them in whole phrases.

53
00:03:08.867 --> 00:03:10.564
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:14.380
Grammar focus: verb plus particle.

55
00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:15.843
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.375
Never give up on your dreams.

57
00:03:19.283 --> 00:03:20.540
He turned it down.

58
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:27.705
Learn phrasal verbs as whole phrases. With a pronoun object, separable verbs put the pronoun in the middle.

59
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.288
Be careful! Don't say: I turned down it.

60
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:35.001
Say: I turned it down.

61
00:03:35.301 --> 00:03:36.476
Pronoun in the middle.

62
00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:39.942
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:41.839
Never Give Up.

64
00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:44.603
Sovann nearly gave up learning English.

65
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.669
His teacher told him to carry on.

66
00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.771
He looked after his little sister at home.

67
00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.765
A joke at the start broke the ice with new friends.

68
00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.952
Now the exam is a piece of cake.

69
00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:02.952
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:03.817 --> 00:04:05.108
Give up means blank.

71
00:04:05.408 --> 00:04:09.154
A, win. B, stop trying. C, start.

72
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.711
The answer is B: stop trying.

73
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:16.956
Turn it blank.

74
00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.468
A, it down. B, downing. C, down.

75
00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.661
The answer is C: down.

76
00:04:26.817 --> 00:04:28.456
Break the ice means blank.

77
00:04:28.756 --> 00:04:33.083
A, start a conversation. B, freeze. C, argue.

78
00:04:36.633 --> 00:04:39.364
The answer is A: start a conversation.

79
00:04:40.517 --> 00:04:42.307
A piece of cake is blank.

80
00:04:42.607 --> 00:04:46.725
A, sweet. B, very easy. C, very hard.

81
00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.568
The answer is B: very easy.

82
00:04:53.717 --> 00:04:55.449
Look after means blank.

83
00:04:55.749 --> 00:04:59.391
A, look at. B, look for. C, take care of.

84
00:05:02.933 --> 00:05:05.119
The answer is C: take care of.

85
00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:09.392
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.563
Use a phrasal verb in a sentence.

87
00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.688
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:31.111
I never give up when a lesson is difficult. I carry on practising until I understand. My teacher says that effort is important.

89
00:05:31.411 --> 00:05:33.236
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:38.532
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb plus particle.

91
00:05:38.832 --> 00:05:43.319
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

92
00:05:43.619 --> 00:05:46.353
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:46.653 --> 00:05:49.816
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

